All four tasks are complete. Summary of what I did and verified:

## E1 — `train.py` code (0 GPU)
- Added `--save-every-epoch` (writes `<stem>.e<N>.pt` per epoch, same `{config, state_dict}` format) and `--tie {earliest,later}` (default `earliest`, so old runs reproduce).
- Factored the tie rule into a torch-free `students/jevlike/selection.py::selection_improves`, imported by `train.py`; `--select acc|nll|nll_t` semantics are unchanged when the new flags are off.
- **Verified:** `python -m unittest tests.test_selection -v` → 7/7 pass (pinned env); `train.py --help` fully imports and shows both new flags.

## E2 — `sweeps/cluster_eval.py` (new, 0 GPU)
Per-cluster accuracy, pass counts (≥95%), and seed mean/range. Output in `sweeps/scratch/v6_clusters.txt` (s7 + s11 on all three splits). Key numbers match the advisor exactly:
- `test_unseen_phrasing`: seed7 0.9960 vs seed11 0.9860; **29 clusters** — the entire gap is `swipe_up "push the screen upward"` (33/33 vs 12/33); 28/29 vs 26/29 pass. Phrases `"previous"` (29/34 vs 28/34) and `"turn it down"` (18/18 vs 17/18).
- `test_unseen_apps`: 0.9940 vs 0.9895; **12 (app, screen) clusters** — 12/12 vs 11/12 (only `docs/document` at 203/214).

## E3 — prob-average ensemble (ran in foreground, 0 GPU)
Elementwise prob mean of s7+s11, scored with `vox.evaluate` → `sweeps/scratch/v6_ens.txt`. I did the **probability average, not weight soup**.
- iid **1.0000**, unseen_phrasing **0.9975**, unseen_apps **0.9945** — ≥ max(seed) on all three splits.

## E4 — `sweeps/scratch/v6s3_queue.sh` (written, NOT run)
Retrains seed 11 as `v6-e5-small-e3-s11b` with `--seed 11 --save-every-epoch --tie later`, then predicts+evaluates the final + each per-epoch checkpoint (`-s11b-e1/-e2/-e3`) on the 3 v6 splits, recording a ledger row per name.

Report written to `sweeps/scratch/v6s3-REPORT.md`.

One note for the coordinator: `train.py` was validated via `--help` + the selection unit tests, but the `--save-every-epoch` checkpoint-writing path was **not** exercised end-to-end (that requires the training run, which is out of scope here). The per-epoch filename in `v6s3_queue.sh` (`runs/sweep-v6-e5-small-e3-s11b.e{N}.pt`) was derived by reading `train.py`'s `out.with_name(f"{out.stem}.e{epoch+1}.pt")`.

